            ["<color=#8A8A93>Research and write-up by Spirit - 'On Damage Types and Buff Activation', University of Rounds. Reproduced for this library with light reformatting; the testing, the findings and the voice are all his.</color>\n\nVia thorough testing in the sandbox game mode with an additional controller player, I have catalogued which types of damage trigger which cards and buffs. The main cards in question are Scavenger, Refresh, Brawler, and Taste of Blood. Lifesteal as a character stat bestowed by numerous cards has also been considered. My results split damage into three main categories: opponent damage, self-damage, and Conditional damage. Damage to your opponent via nearly any means will trigger all cards and buffs, with the exception of specific types of Conditional damage. For various reasons, some Conditional damage, typically from block cards, will not consistently trigger Refresh but will still trigger all other buffs. Finally, any form of self-damage will always activate Scavenger, but nothing else. There are, of course, numerous oddities and exceptions.\n\n<color=#FFD94D><b>THE TABLE OF DAMAGE INTERACTIONS</b></color>\n\nColumns: Scav = Scavenger, Brawl = Brawler, ToB = Taste of Blood, Steal = lifesteal, Refr = Refresh. Cond = triggers conditionally (explained below).\n\n<color=#FFD94D>Damage source<pos=34%>Scav<pos=45%>Brawl<pos=56%>ToB<pos=67%>Steal<pos=78%>Refr</color>\nBullet damage<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Yes\nBullet damage (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nAbyssal Countdown<pos=34%>No<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nBombs Away<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nBombs Away (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nDecay<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nDecay (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nDemonic Pact (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nDemonic Pact (AoE)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nEMP<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nEMP (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nExplosive Bullet<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nExplosive Bullet (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nFrost Slam<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>No\nLifestealer<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nOverpower<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Yes\nParasite<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nParasite (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nPoison<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nPoison (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nRadiance<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nSaw<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nShield Charge<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Yes\nSilence<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nShockwave<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>No\nStatic Field<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nSupernova<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Yes\nTimed Detonation<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nTimed Detonation (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\nToxic Cloud<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>Yes<pos=56%>Yes<pos=67%>Yes<pos=78%>Cond\nToxic Cloud (self)<pos=34%>Yes<pos=45%>No<pos=56%>No<pos=67%>No<pos=78%>No\n\nAll of these tests were carried out in the sandbox gamemode using two players, one on keyboard, the other on controller. Each test was repeated multiple times to ensure the results were consistent, or at least consistently inconsistent. No distinction was made between Timed Detonation AoE damage latched onto a player vs latched onto a surface.\n\nPromising potential damage dealers, such as Chilling Presence, were excluded due to both their failure to trigger any cards or buffs and their failure to deal any damage. Every entry on the list deals damage in some form, and every unique way to deal damage has an entry. Thus, there are no methods to trigger any damage-dealing cards or buffs without dealing some amount of damage. That might seem obvious but, given the weirdness of the rest of the system, one can never be too sure."] = "<color=#8A8A93>Forskning och text av Spirit - 'On Damage Types and Buff Activation', University of Rounds. Återgiven för det här biblioteket med lätt omformatering; testerna, slutsatserna och rösten är helt och hållet hans.</color>\n\nGenom grundliga tester i sandbox-läget med en extra handkontrollspelare har jag katalogiserat vilka typer av skada som aktiverar vilka kort och buffar. Korten i fråga är främst Scavenger, Refresh, Brawler och Taste of Blood. Livsstöld som karaktärsstat, given av åtskilliga kort, har också tagits med. Mina resultat delar upp skadan i tre huvudkategorier: motståndarskada, självskada och villkorlig skada. Skada på din motståndare på nästan vilket sätt som helst aktiverar alla kort och buffar, med undantag för vissa typer av villkorlig skada. Av olika skäl kommer viss villkorlig skada, oftast från blockkort, inte att konsekvent aktivera Refresh men ändå aktivera alla andra buffar. Slutligen aktiverar varje form av självskada alltid Scavenger, men inget annat. Det finns förstås gott om egenheter och undantag.\n\n<color=#FFD94D><b>TABELLEN ÖVER SKADEINTERAKTIONER</b></color>\n\nKolumner: Scav = Scavenger, Brawl = Brawler, ToB = Taste of Blood, Steal = livsstöld, Refr = Refresh. Villk = aktiveras villkorligt (förklaras nedan).\n\n<color=#FFD94D>Skadekälla<pos=34%>Scav<pos=45%>Brawl<pos=56%>ToB<pos=67%>Steal<pos=78%>Refr</color>\nKulskada<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Ja\nKulskada (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nAbyssal Countdown<pos=34%>Nej<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nBombs Away<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nBombs Away (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nDecay<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nDecay (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nDemonic Pact (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nDemonic Pact (AoE)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nEMP<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nEMP (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nExplosive Bullet<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nExplosive Bullet (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nFrost Slam<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Nej\nLifestealer<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nOverpower<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Ja\nParasite<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nParasite (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nPoison<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nPoison (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nRadiance<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nSaw<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nShield Charge<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Ja\nSilence<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nShockwave<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Nej\nStatic Field<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nSupernova<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Ja\nTimed Detonation<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nTimed Detonation (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\nToxic Cloud<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Ja<pos=56%>Ja<pos=67%>Ja<pos=78%>Villk\nToxic Cloud (själv)<pos=34%>Ja<pos=45%>Nej<pos=56%>Nej<pos=67%>Nej<pos=78%>Nej\n\nAlla dessa tester genomfördes i sandbox-läget med två spelare, en på tangentbord och en på handkontroll. Varje test upprepades flera gånger för att säkerställa att resultaten var konsekventa, eller åtminstone konsekvent inkonsekventa. Ingen skillnad gjordes mellan Timed Detonation-AoE-skada fäst på en spelare och fäst på en yta.\n\nLovande potentiella skadegörare, som Chilling Presence, uteslöts både för att de inte aktiverade några kort eller buffar och för att de inte gjorde någon skada. Varje post på listan gör skada i någon form, och varje unikt sätt att göra skada har en post. Det finns alltså inga sätt att aktivera skadeutlösta kort eller buffar utan att göra någon mängd skada. Det kan låta självklart, men med tanke på hur konstigt resten av systemet är kan man aldrig vara riktigt säker.",
